---
title: Sandwich Loaf
author: Mildred McKinzie
category: Casseroles
cook time: 20 minutes
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@unsliced bread{1%loaf}
@hard-boiled eggs{4} (chopped)
@sliced stuffed olives{1/3%cup}
@chopped onion{1.5%tsp}
@salad dressing
@tuna{1%can}
@grated cheese{1%cup}
@butter

Trim off crust from 1 loaf unsliced bread. Cut in 4 layers lengthwise. Butter each layer on one side. Mix chopped hard-boiled eggs, sliced stuffed olives, chopped onion, tuna, and grated cheese. Moisten with salad dressing. Fill layers and stack them 1 inch thick. Butter all sides and wrap in tin foil. Bake at 420 degrees for 20 minutes.
